# Image Handling

Use `TechnoSapiens\Core\Image::render()` to output `<img>` or `<picture>` with BEM classes and responsive markup. Follow `sections/section-content`.

## Get the image from ACF

`section-content` stores the image as an **array** and reads `ID`:

```php
use TechnoSapiens\Core\Image;

$contentImage = get_field('content_image') ?? [];
$contentImageId = !empty($contentImage['ID']) ? (int) $contentImage['ID'] : 0;
```

## Render

```php
<?php if ($contentImageId) : ?>
    <figure class="section-content__figure">
        <?php echo Image::render([
            'blockClass' => 'section-content',
            'sources' => [
                [
                    'id' => $contentImageId,
                    'size' => 'full',
                ],
            ],
        ]); ?>
    </figure>
<?php endif; ?>
```

`blockClass` becomes the BEM prefix (`section-content__image`).

`Image::render()` fills `alt` from `Image::altFromId()` when omitted (attachment alt, then title). Informative images: omit `alt` or pass real text. Decorative images: `'alt' => ''` so screen readers skip them — do not keep the filename fallback.

## Responsive sources

```php
echo Image::render([
    'blockClass' => 'section-hero',
    'lazy' => true,
    'sources' => [
        [
            'id' => $imageDesktopId,
            'size' => 'full',
            'media' => '(min-width: 481px)',
        ],
        [
            'id' => $imageMobileId,
            'size' => 'full',
            'media' => '(min-width: 0px)',
        ],
    ],
]);
```

Register extra sizes with `add_image_size()` in theme `initImageSizes()` or the section class constructor only when the design needs cropped sizes. `section-content` uses `'full'`.

## `Image::render()` parameters

**Global:** `blockClass`, `class`, `lazy` (default true), `draggable`, `decoding`, `alt`, `style`

**Per source:** `id`, `url`, `size`, `size2x`, `media`, `width`, `height`, `alt`
